---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy — Olgierd Stach">
  <main id="main" class="shell prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</p>
    <h1>
      A small amount of data,
      <br />
      for a clear purpose.
    </h1>
    <p>
      If you select Yes in the resume download form, this site stores your
      company name, a random request identifier, and the request time to
      understand recruiting interest. Do not enter personal information in the
      company field.
    </p>
    <p>
      The record expires after 30 days. DynamoDB deletes expired records
      asynchronously, typically within a few days. Selecting No does not create
      a recruiting-interest record. Both options require a security check before
      the download API returns the PDF.
    </p>
    <p>
      The application does not store your IP address, browser information, email
      address, or name. Infrastructure providers necessarily process connection
      information to deliver the website. Application logs do not include
      submitted company names or request bodies.
    </p>
    <p>
      Opening the download dialog loads Cloudflare Turnstile to help prevent
      automated downloads. Cloudflare processes browser and connection
      information for this check. The backend verifies its short-lived token;
      the application does not store that token. See{' '}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">
        Cloudflare's privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      Certificate images are served by this website. Following a verification
      link takes you to the certificate provider and its privacy policy. No
      Credly scripts or embeds are loaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      For questions or deletion requests, contact the site owner through the
      public <a href="https://github.com/OStach-adm01">GitHub profile</a>. Do
      not publish personal details in a public issue.
    </p>
    <a href="/" class="text-link">
      ← Back to the website
    </a>
  </main>
</Layout>
